\section{RStudio}{

Setting breakpoints inside \code{oopr} classes is the same process as setting
them for normal functions - use the gutter or \code{SHIFT+F9}.

RStudio calls its R functions inside \code{tools:rstudio} from the global
environment. By assigning functions of the same name, these calls can be
intercepted.

This feature is disabled by default as it is potentially destructive for
an R session. Environmental variable \code{R_OOPR_BREAKPOINTS=true} can be used
to enable this functionality when \code{oopr} namespace is loaded.

Breakpoints cannot be set on single line functions with a specifier,

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{get:x <- \\( ) \{ return("x"); \}
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

as RStudio thinks the line is at the top-level.

Tested with RStudio version 2026.1.1.403, there are no guarantees for
earlier or later versions.
}

\section{\ht{OoprBreakpointsImpl-OoprBreakpointsRStudio}{OoprBreakpointsRStudio}\hr\hr{}OoprBreakpointsRStudio}{

\subsection{Description}{
\lbr{}The controller for RStudio breakpoints.
}

\subsection{Details}{
\lbr{}RStudio's process of setting a breakpoint is:
\enumerate{
\item Check the function is in sync.
\item Get the steps of the functions body to arrive at a line.
\item Get the environment that the function is assigned to.
\item Set the breakpoints into the function.
Only steps 3 & 4 apply when unsetting a breakpoint, or reloading a file.
}

RStudio maintains its own record of breakpoints and is recorded by
file and function name. However, multiple classes in a file could share a
function name.

TODO: newer versions of RStudio use \code{.rs.setBreakpoint}.
}

\subsection{Methods}{
\describe{
\item{\command{\hl{OoprBreakpointsImpl-OoprBreakpointsRStudio-isFunctionInSync}{isFunctionInSync}}}{
\emph{\verb{[static]}} \cr
Checks whether the srcref matches the file.}

\item{\command{\hl{OoprBreakpointsImpl-OoprBreakpointsRStudio-getFunctionSteps}{getFunctionSteps}}}{
\emph{\verb{[static]}} \cr
Gets the "steps" required for a line.}

\item{\command{\hl{OoprBreakpointsImpl-OoprBreakpointsRStudio-getEnvironmentOfFunction}{getEnvironmentOfFunction}}}{
\emph{\verb{[static]}} \cr
Gets the environment of a function.}

\item{\command{\hl{OoprBreakpointsImpl-OoprBreakpointsRStudio-setFunctionBreakpoints}{setFunctionBreakpoints}}}{
\emph{\verb{[static]}} \cr
Sets the breakpoints for a function.}
}
}

